## Next Task — Enable Product Image Galleries

### Objective

Introduce configurable product image galleries in the storefront.

### Gallery configuration

There will be **three gallery styles** available:

**1. Default gallery — mandatory**

The default gallery style will always be available.

**2. Optional Gallery Style #1**

Additional gallery presentation style.

**3. Optional Gallery Style #2**

Additional gallery presentation style.

The two additional styles should be **feature-configurable**, rather than hard-coded as universally enabled functionality.

Conceptually:

```text
Product Image Gallery
        │
        ├── Default Style
        │     └── Always available
        │
        ├── Optional Style 1
        │     └── Feature configurable
        │
        └── Optional Style 2
              └── Feature configurable
```

### Important architectural principle

Gallery **presentation** should remain separate from the underlying product image data.

In other words:

```text
Product Images
      ↓
Gallery Configuration
      ↓
Selected Gallery Style
      ↓
Gallery Renderer
```

The feature configuration should determine which gallery capabilities are available, while the renderer determines how the images are presented.

